From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 08:00:31 -0400
Subject: feat: the sidebar on the right (S-96)

"Sidebar on the right" (stedding.sidebar.on_right, the side on screen)
moves the sidebar to the window's right in every window of the profile at
once, private windows included. It is set from Settings > Stedding >
Sidebar, the sidebar's own menu, the Mac's View menu and the command bar.

The layout places the strip at the window's trailing edge by a flag
(VerticalTabStripRegionView::IsAtTrailingEdge) instead of mirroring the
browser view, so the page's native surface and the layers follow a live
switch; six marked hunks in the tabbed layout. The handle and its bar,
the rail's centre, the reveal edge, the drop arrow and the hover cards
mirror. The Mac's traffic lights stay at the top left over the address
row; Windows' caption buttons sit over the sidebar's top row in its
colours, and the rail's toggle drops below them. On the right the reveal
edge is the window's last 2 DIP with a 300 ms rest, and a press drops a
pending reveal, so the page's scroll bar stays usable. The address row's
caption reserve is worked out once per layout, so the toolbar centres on
the reserve the layout used.

Rows: sidebar Y34-Y43, menus M13, settings T33, commandbar K35. A new
patch after 0088 in the series.

Why: BACKLOG S-96 (ROADMAP M10) asks for the sidebar on the window's
right as a setting.
Removable when: the setting is withdrawn from the product; until then the
layout flag and its tests stay together.
